    "result_text": "The test passes. The change is complete as a full-stack, additive implementation:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V10__invoice_due_date_index.sql`: new additive migration adding an index on `invoice.due_date` to back the sort ordering.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST):\n- `InvoiceRepository` \u2014 added `findAllByOrderByDueDateAscIdAsc()` (earliest due first, id as stable tiebreaker).\n- `InvoicesGet` \u2014 now reads an optional `sort` query param; `sort=due` returns the due-date-ordered list, otherwise the existing stable oldest-first order. No new endpoint/router; the existing `/api/invoices` route is extended.\n\n**Front-end** (all new files except the panel reading the shared key):\n- `slots/defs/invoicesToolbar.ts` \u2014 new slot region above the invoices table.\n- `features/invoices/sortByDue.slot.tsx` \u2014 self-contained control with `data-testid=\"invoice-sort-due\"`, owning the `invoiceSort` URL search param (rule 4 \u2014 state that outlives a click lives in the URL).\n- `features/invoices/InvoicesPanel.tsx` \u2014 renders the new toolbar slot and reads the same `invoiceSort` key, folding it into its `['invoices', sort]` query key and request. The key still starts with `invoices`, so existing create/pay invalidations keep refreshing it. Server data stays the single source of truth \u2014 nothing re-sorted or copied by hand.\n\nExisting `data-testid`s (`invoice-row-*`, `invoice-due`, etc.) are untouched. Typecheck and the Playwright acceptance spec both pass.",
